node_modules/
dist/

# Local-only agent files. These name the operator's private LAN, paths and hardware; this repo is
# PUBLIC. They must never be committed — see the "Public-repo hygiene" rule in CLAUDE.local.md.
#
# NOTE: `CLAUDE.md` itself IS committed and public — it is what a coding agent reads on a fresh
# clone to set the project up, so ignoring it would defeat the point. Anything environment-specific
# belongs in CLAUDE.local.md, which every agent also reads and which never leaves this machine.
CLAUDE.local.md
GEMINI.md
AGENTS.md
docs/TechDebt.md
docs/HANDOFF.md
docs/TODO.md

# `npm run audit:prompts` output — records LOCAL absolute paths, so it must never be committed.
ayin-prompts-audit.json

# Artifacts ayin writes into whatever directory it RUNS IN — including this one, when used on itself.
# `src/watch.ts` already maintained this inventory for its own staging filter and it never reached here,
# which is exactly how a generated file carrying absolute local paths got committed. A plan file embeds
# the verbatim prompt, the goal and absolute paths by construction.
ayin-plan-*.md
ayin-explain-*.md
AYIN-REPORT-*.md
reviews/
*.puml
*.invalid.puml
